# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

This resource allows you to create and configure an AppResource object in ConductorOne.
When creating an AppResource you must provide a display name, app_id and app_resource_type_id. Optionally, you can provide a description.

## Destroy behavior

Destroying this resource deletes the app resource only if it was created in ConductorOne and is not managed by a connector (`is_manually_managed = true`).
If the app resource is managed by a connector (for example, it was adopted or merged with a connector-synced row via `match_baton_id`), Terraform does not delete it. Instead `terraform destroy` **releases** it: Terraform removes it from state and emits a warning, but leaves it unchanged in ConductorOne, where the connector keeps it in sync. Applying the configuration again adopts the same ID.
If the app resource is already gone, destroy succeeds without calling the API to delete it.

